Important and Urgent, Do (your MVP)

Add a course with named grading categories and their weights, with a check that the weights add up to 100 percent
Enter scores for completed assignments inside each category
Calculate the current grade for every course using a weighted average of the completed work
Target grade calculator that tells you what average you need on the remaining work to hit a chosen grade
Rank upcoming assignments by how much each one can move your final grade
Save and load courses from a local text file so you do not retype everything each run

Important but Not Urgent, Schedule (V2.0+)

Due dates for each assignment, with the ranking combining impact and how soon it is due
Support for syllabus rules like “drop the lowest quiz” or extra credit
What-if mode that lets you test a hypothetical score and see the new grade
Weekly workload summary that suggests where to spend study time
Custom letter grade scales and a semester GPA estimate

Urgent but Not Important, Delegate (use a library)

Reading and writing the save file in JSON using a library like Gson instead of hand-rolled parsing
Handling dates with Java’s built-in java.time package
Parsing command line commands and flags with a library like picocli
Printing clean tables in the terminal with a small text table library

Not Important and Not Urgent, Delete (cut it)

A GUI/web app
Automatic import of grades from Brightspace or Gradescope, which would need logins and unofficial APIs
Reading syllabus PDFs automatically to fill in the weights
User accounts, cloud sync, or sharing grades with friends
